{"decision":"fix","task_id":"BUG-05","summary":"Retry guard no longer blocks repeated identical failing attempts; the new touched-files check lets the infinite-loop case pass through and tests still fail.","quality_score":61,"issues":["`src/ralph/resources/ralph.sh` changed the block condition to require a non-empty post-review `CURRENT_DIFF`, but in the real failing-loop case the lead resets the wrong patch before the comparison, so attempt 2 can still be the same bad work while `CURRENT_DIFF` is empty and the task incorrectly reaches `verified_done`. This breaks the existing retry-block behavior and leaves `tests/test_integration.py::test_ralph_blocks_retry_when_attempt_diff_matches_previous_attempt` failing."],"fix_instructions":"Keep the noop-retry allowance, but make the retry guard decide from attempt-level evidence captured before the reset rather than from the post-reset diff alone. In `src/ralph/resources/ralph.sh`, persist whether the current coder attempt actually reproduced the same task-scoped patch as the prior attempt, then block when the two attempt patches match even if the lead reset leaves `CURRENT_DIFF` empty. This should preserve the new `attempt 1 changed, attempt 2 noop` pass case while restoring the block expected by `tests/test_integration.py::test_ralph_blocks_retry_when_attempt_diff_matches_previous_attempt` and the failed retry-context test.","alert_reason":"","progress_note":"Implementation is close, but acceptance is not met because the genuine identical-retry loop is no longer detected."}
END_RALPH_REVIEW_JSON
